sharedHelperNeeded:
YES — one shared overlay-scoping helper on StudioEditorViewModel, used by all three render surfaces (canvas, overlay-timeline lane, export/scopedSnapshot). It must bridge the clipID -> sessionMediaID key mismatch, so filterByMedia (which keys on sessionMediaID) CANNOT be reused as-is. Recommended exact form (resolve via `snapshot.clips`, NOT `visibleSnapshotClips`, so the helper can still find an in-scope clip while scoping is active):

private func overlayInScope(_ ov: OverlayItem) -> Bool {
    guard let visible = visibleClipMediaIDs else { return true }   // unscoped workout view: show all
    guard let clipID = ov.clipID else { return true }              // whole-project overlay (text/sticker/no-selection climb tag): show in every scope
    guard let clip = snapshot.clips.first(where: { $0.id == clipID }),
          let mediaID = clip.sessionMediaID else { return false }   // orphan/foreign: hide when scoping
    return visible.contains(mediaID)
}
private var scopedOverlays: [OverlayItem] { snapshot.overlays.filter(overlayInScope) }

Equivalent id-bridge form also acceptable: `let ids = Set(visibleSnapshotClips.map(\.id)); ov.clipID.map(ids.contains) ?? true` (maps clipID against visible TimelineClip ids). Either is correct; the sessionMediaID form above is the most literal map of clipID->owning clip->sessionMediaID->membership. Add a pure unit test: two clips each with a climb tag, scope=[mediaA] yields only clipA's tag (plus any clipID==nil overlay) in canvasOverlays/timelineOverlays; ideally extract a pure `StudioGeometry.filterOverlays(_:visibleClipIDs:)` so it tests without a device.
